{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition","id":474023,"title":"State of Anathema for Third Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-09T03:38:28-07:00","id":474023,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> State of Anathema for Third Edition","content":"This is Urs from Anathema.<br /> <br /> There was some discontent over the lack of news lately, way over in another thread.<br /> In this post, I'll try to remedy the situation and give you some insight into our collaboration with Onyx Path as well as our progress. Please understand that I can't go into details; I am NDAed and can only speak about the general outline.<br /> <br /> Our main contact in the writing team is Holden. We are in close contact with him, meaning: unmoderated, direct, private messages.<br /> Some weeks ago, he sent us a pre-release version of the rules, more than enough to build Anathema with.<br /> He answers any questions we have clearly and quickly, and generally does his best to keep us in the loop.<br /> Just to make it clear, Onyx Path is not responsible for our doings, errors or lapses, as we are not beholden to them. We did not ask for money, and will receive none. In fact, we - as a team - explictly decided not to make this a paid project, so we never had to discuss this with OP.<br /> <br /> Rules in hand, we obviously have a lot of work to do, reading as well as coding.<br /> Generally speaking, work is progressing orderly. We are working in a hidden repository, that's why even the tech-savvy among you didn't see any updates on GitHub for ages. Progress could be better, though, since our time and energy are not as plenty as they were back in 2013, when we first signed up for this.<br /> I have seen speculation that we only need to update the Charms - this is decidedly not the case, the changes required are much more extensive: There are assumptions in Anathema that just don't hold any longer, and we still need to figure out how to deal with a few major points.<br /> However, all of the minor changes and additions are done by now. With a version I have running on my desktop this very moment, I could probably adopt more than eighty percent of the Exalts I or my group have played in the past; dealing with some rough edges manually.<br /> <br /> All of this said, we can't promise to have a fully-fledged version the moment the PDF goes live - just as I said back in September.<br /> Also, OP and the Anathema team have yet to speak about content inclusion beyond the usual - we have left this issue open so far, because it is the least of our concerns.<br /> <br /> Finally, please bear in mind that Rich knows exactly as much about our work as you do, so he just couldn't give you more details.<br /> <br /> I hope this clears matters up somewhat.<br /> If you have any questions, please post below. I will try to answer them as good as I can.<br /> <br /> UPDATE: We have solved one of the puzzles mentioned above.<br /> UPDATE: Solved another puzzle. It gets harder from here on out.<br /> UPDATE: The code is now public. We needed to clean out the Charm data before publishing. Release is still some time off, as the puzzlers are unresolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","user":"urskr","date":".  UPDATE 3 11-24-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":46}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T03:57:05-07:00","id":474049,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the information and keep up the good work. You can take all the time you need in my opinion. I just hope it works well when it's finally released, and I have no doubts that it's going to be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T03:57:56-07:00","id":474053,"title":"","content":"Appreciate the update. Would be great if more content (charm wise) could be included, but understand that as it is a not paid for product that might not be too palatable to the license holders.<br /> <br /> It would be a great boon to me as an ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1181-molez","name":"Molez","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1181_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:09:01-07:00","id":474057,"title":"","content":"Sounds good, thanks for the heads up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:50:24-07:00","id":474094,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the update, Urs. I am a little surprised to see that this isn't a paid-for project (as I had assumed), but I can see why the IP owner (CCP) would be hesitant to do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Molez</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474053#post474053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Appreciate the update. Would be great if more content (charm wise) could be included, but understand that as it is a not paid for product that might not be too palatable to the license holders.<br /> <br /> It would be a great boon to me as an ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to what you are referring to. Like, more charms than what's going to be in the book, or as in antagonist charms also included in the program? My greatest boon from Anathema was being able to make new player's characters for them. Such that we could sit down and talk about what they wanted to play, and I could basically interview them, and while doing so draw up a character sheet that was then printable.<br /> As long as I can do that (or even just character management software, even if it isn't exportable), I'm a happy camper. :-D<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>ST/DM for <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCfFy7kNgMvxIR1qdzT8PzEg\" target=\"_blank\">Dice Alternatives</a><br /> Playing: <a href=\"http://causality-and-consequences.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">DtD: Causality and Consequence</a><br /> Off-Season: <a href=\"http://lifelong-educations.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">M:tAw- Lifelong Education</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/667-abenniton","name":"ABenniton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar667_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T04:59:14-07:00","id":474122,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure he meant that he would like the full text of Charms to be available (obviously a CCP/OP decision, not Anathema).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5411-andrewh","name":"AndrewH","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T05:28:42-07:00","id":474135,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the update! Looking forward to seeing this on my computer whenever it does release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T08:31:18-07:00","id":474326,"title":"","content":"Question: Will this be only the character creation or will there be the campaign and storytellers parts included in the release?<br /> <br /> Question: Will you have a conversion option to take a character from 2nd to 3rd are we going to have to redo our characters we in the current release?<br /> <br /> Question: Will the release of Anathema have mortals as well as solars or will there be a wait for that?<br /> <br /> Question: Will you be using the stock character sheet or will there be a custom design. Or will there be a option to choose between stock and custom?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:52:47-07:00","id":474421,"title":"","content":"Will the earlier edition versions of Anathema (1e, 2e, 2.5e) still be available?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:39:17-07:00","id":474481,"title":"","content":"Oh, thank you for the update! Looking forward to fiddling with your builder when it comes out, should be a blast!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:11:51-07:00","id":474661,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that update! It's really kind of you to keep us in the loop. I hope to see the result of your work soon, so I can congratulate you all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:29:53-07:00","id":474699,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the news update. ^_^ I didn't actually try Anathema during 2e (what with not really finding out about it until I'd given up on playing), but I've heard enough good things that I'm looking forward to changing that for the upcoming edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:36:12-07:00","id":474704,"title":"","content":"I basically can't play Exalted without using Anathema anymore, so I really appreciate all the work you're putting in to making it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:44:42-07:00","id":474720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474326#post474326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: Will this be only the character creation or will there be the campaign and storytellers parts included in the release?</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be character management, that is, creation and growth.<br /> Our ideas for campaign and storyteller support never really took off, part because we were busy enough supporting the myriad options Exalted has to offer, part because we just don't know what a should go there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question: Will you have a conversion option to take a character from 2nd to 3rd are we going to have to redo our characters we in the current release? </div> </div> </div>We do not plan to include a conversion option. Reasons are both technical and in the effort required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question: Will the release of Anathema have mortals as well as solars or will there be a wait for that? </div> </div> </div>Both. As far as I remember, Mortals are completely done already, and a release without Solars just wouldn't make much sense, since that is where the complexity lies.<br /> At this stage, I won't rule out an early-access version with mortals only to get feedback on certain UI decisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Question: Will you be using the stock character sheet or will there be a custom design. Or will there be a option to choose between stock and custom? </div> </div> </div>We have offered custom sheets based on voidstates layouts for time immemorial, and will continue to do so. I expect them to be similar to what we have, with obvious changes for 3e.<br /> If somebody brings us code to print into the stock sheet, we'll take it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T12:46:03-07:00","id":474721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474421#post474421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will the earlier edition versions of Anathema (1e, 2e, 2.5e) still be available?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, as they are right now. Our support will be limited to answering questions, though - if anyone wants to take over maintenance, he or she is welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:12:10-07:00","id":474795,"title":"","content":"Do you have plans on improving extensibility options through external definitions ? Much like the addition of custom charms but applying to more attributes than just charms, including new keywords, new exalt types, etc ? If attributes, dependencies and definitions aren't hard coded in, you not only have options for homebrew but crowd sourcing beyond those that know their way around git/gradle !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:21:10-07:00","id":474808,"title":"","content":"Any chance you'll squeeze an Exalted Name Generator in there? Voidstats name gen was super useful until his site went dark and was lost to the internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5618-quorumof4","name":"QuorumOf4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:38:35-07:00","id":474876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474795#post474795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have plans on improving extensibility options through external definitions? Much like the addition of custom charms but applying to more attributes than just charms, including new keywords, new exalt types, etc ? If attributes, dependencies and definitions aren't hard coded in, you not only have options for homebrew but crowd sourcing beyond those that know their way around git/gradle !</div> </div> </div> </div>The current platform has much less hardcoded content than previous editions. Whether this scratches your particular itch only time will tell. These days, we try to hardcode as few assumptions as possible, but at times, it is hard to notice - and at certain points, &quot;just hardcode it&quot; is a very reasonable decision: It is an order of magnitude easier than writing a fully generic rules engine for variations that we do not yet know about.<br /> Even though, we'll still prefer pull requests via github over raw files sent in by email.<br /> <br /> I have extracted a very technical sample of the extent of configuration for character types below.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> The type definition. You can remove or exchange each of the models with no harm done, as long as no other models depend on them.<br /> Free raises for all abilities? Remove the line. Different starting health levels? Make a new template and change the definition. (See below)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">{ characterType: Solar; template: Lawgiver; models: { Description:'', Points: SolarPoints, Concept: SolarCastes, SpiritualTraits:SolarSpiritualTraits, SpiritualPoints:SolarSpiritualPoints, Abilities: SolarAbilities, AbilitiesPoints: SolarAbilityPoints, Attributes: DefaultAttributes, AttributePoints: SolarAttributePoints, EssencePool: SolarEssencePool, Health: SolarHealth, ...more of the same... } }</pre> </div>And this is the health definition for Solars. Please say this is cool.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">{ levels: &#91;-0,-1,-1,-2,-2,-4,Incapacitated&#93; }</pre> </div>As a more complex example, this is the definition of &quot;Default Attributes&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_description\">Code:</div> <pre class=\"bbcode_code notranslate\" style=\"max-height:calc(30 * 1.4rem + 2 * var(--bbcode-padding) + var(--h-scrollbar-allowance));\">{ groups: &#91; { id: &quot;Physical&quot;, traits: &#91;&quot;Strength&quot;, &quot;Dexterity&quot;, &quot;Stamina&quot;&#93; }, { id: &quot;Social&quot;, traits: &#91;&quot;Charisma&quot;, &quot;Manipulation&quot;, &quot;Appearance&quot;&#93; }, { id: &quot;Mental&quot;, traits: &#91;&quot;Perception&quot;, &quot;Intelligence&quot;, &quot;Wits&quot;&#93; } &#93;; standard: { startValue: 1; minimumValue = 1; modificationType: &quot;RaiseOnly&quot;; limitation: { type: &quot;Essence&quot; } } }</pre> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","user":"urskr","date":".  You can now change attributes. 04-19-2015, 03:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:50:48-07:00","id":474884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuorumOf4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474808#post474808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance you'll squeeze an Exalted Name Generator in there? Voidstats name gen was super useful until his site went dark and was lost to the internet.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is to say: We already have one, even based on voidstate's data. Ours might be the last surviving copy of voidstate's tables that is openly available.<br /> [SHAMELESSPLUG]Apart from my own side project, that is. If you like Exalted and random stuff, you could do worse than following <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=anathema.android\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a>.[/SHAMELESSPLUG]<br /> Our realm name generator isn't as good, though, I mean to rewrite it at some point using Tobias Bindslet's scripts as inspiration.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:48:34-07:00","id":474991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474876#post474876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The current platform has much less hardcoded content than previous editions. Whether this scratches your particular itch only time will tell. These days, we try to hardcode as few assumptions as possible, but at times, it is hard to notice - and at certain points, &quot;just hardcode it&quot; is a very reasonable decision: It is an order of magnitude easier than writing a fully generic rules engine for variations that we do not yet know about.<br /> Even though, we'll still prefer pull requests via github over raw files sent in by email.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would this mean that it might be modular enough that Onyx Path could, potentially, at some point decide to sell a module that would add the full charm texts to the free Anathema base?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:18:18-07:00","id":475039,"title":"","content":"That looks quite encouraging to me ! So as long as characters follow the same general structure (they have attributes and abilities, etc) then it shouldn't be a terribly difficult task to fan-update old ones or create your new. Hiccups I'm seeing would be something like Rakasha, with their fancy new core values like Cups/etc.; you can always bandaid it by utilizing backgrounds/merits, although I can only speculate on how dependencies would work. It seems neat so far =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:22:41-07:00","id":475045,"title":"","content":"OHh, and a suggestion for custom character sheet templates ? It's a little on the fidgety side but you could try working with pdf's fdf format ? Various PDF styles to represent the different looks and feel that all reference the same .fdf file structure ? This would only represent a common output format though on the PDF print outputs and Acrobat is notoriously fussy when it comes to those elements. You'd have to get down into the weeds when it comes to pdf coding to wrangle any consistency out of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:54:04-07:00","id":475113,"title":"","content":"1. Will you be including one UI or several that can be switched between?<br /> <br /> 2. Will there be one set of art skins or several that can be switched between?<br /> <br /> 3. Without giving any NDA-no-no details, on a scale of 1 to yourheadasplode, how awesome is the new ruleset?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 04-09-2015, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T18:36:20-07:00","id":475184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475113#post475113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Without giving any NDA-no-no details, on a scale of 1 to yourheadasplode, how awesome is the new ruleset?</div> </div> </div> </div>My own answer would be <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=80DtQD5BQ_A&amp;t=1m52s\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:11:49-07:00","id":475391,"title":"","content":"Grand. Can't remember the last time I said that and it wasn't sarcastic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T00:53:34-07:00","id":475500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474991#post474991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would this mean that it might be modular enough that Onyx Path could, potentially, at some point decide to sell a module that would add the full charm texts to the free Anathema base?</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. This road has been open ever since we introduced the option to add custom Charm text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475045#post475045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little on the fidgety side but you could try working with pdf's fdf format ? Various PDF styles to represent the different looks and feel that all reference the same .fdf file structure ? This would only represent a common output format though on the PDF print outputs and Acrobat is notoriously fussy when it comes to those elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>We currently don't plan to re-write the sheet encoding, so I don't think we'll go there. As always, contributions are welcome, but in this case I'd love to know where you see the advantage over what we currently do: building the vectors and text elements for the PDF in Java code based on the character's traits and properties.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475113#post475113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Will you be including one UI or several that can be switched between?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure what you mean by an &quot;UI&quot; - I thought it's a &quot;skin&quot; until I read the question below. Please clarify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Will there be one set of art skins or several that can be switched between? </div> </div> </div>Tough question. We've always done a little reskinning for the various character types. We'll keep doing that.<br /> Otherwise, Anathema will look the same no matter whether you play a Mortal or a Solar.<br /> However, our new UI toolkit allows for extensive CSS styling, so if anybody feels up to the task: Let's talk!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Without giving any NDA-no-no details, on a scale of 1 to yourheadasplode, how awesome is the new ruleset? </div> </div> </div>It's Exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T05:52:30-07:00","id":475666,"title":"","content":"When Anathema is done, is there any talks about maybe doing a nWod/oWod system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T06:01:21-07:00","id":475675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475500#post475500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what's its splat?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T06:17:29-07:00","id":475718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475500#post475500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We currently don't plan to re-write the sheet encoding, so I don't think we'll go there. As always, contributions are welcome, but in this case I'd love to know where you see the advantage over what we currently do: building the vectors and text elements for the PDF in Java code based on the character's traits and properties.<br /> <br /> It's Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>A boring, but useful example is a tax form. You have lots of fillable fields to type numbers and text into and depending on the settings of the document (Acrobat is .. weird about it's permission sets), you can save the text you typed in which gets outputted as a .fdf file. All the data in this fdf file relates to the names of fields in the pdf rather than positioning within pdf document. The PDF determines where that field is drawn and the FDF determines what the contents of that editable field is. The idea in this case would be to come up with a PDF agnostic FDF output. Then, so long as the field mappings were done correctly, you could have any number of PDF documents. They all might have the &quot;Name&quot; and &quot;Str Attribute&quot; fields, but where and how they're drawn depends on the individual PDF. What this effectively does is allow you to template the final printout without having to worry about drawing different character sheets in your own software. All you'd need to worry about is the encoded form data that plugs into various other character sheet PDF documents.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lets say someone gifted in design comes up with a fantastic new character sheet layout. What you could do is take their PDF, use PDF editing software to add the proper fields in the proper placement and now it's all set utilize the output you'd already be generating for other PDF templates, requiring no change in Anethema's code to accommodate the new layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1759,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","user":"kawaiiwolf","date":". 04-10-2015, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:18:34-07:00","id":475926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475666#post475666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Anathema is done, is there any talks about maybe doing a nWod/oWod system?</div> </div> </div> </div>There might be some legal complications there since Herolab already does the nWoD module. I would expect (but I don't know) that such commercial arrangements are usually somewhat exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:06:32-07:00","id":475979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=474884#post474884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ukd5y2z-ORA </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is to say: We already have one, even based on voidstate's data. Ours might be the last surviving copy of voidstate's tables that is openly available.<br /> [SHAMELESSPLUG]Apart from my own side project, that is. If you like Exalted and random stuff, you could do worse than following <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=anathema.android\" target=\"_blank\">this link</a>.[/SHAMELESSPLUG]<br /> Our realm name generator isn't as good, though, I mean to rewrite it at some point using Tobias Bindslet's scripts as inspiration.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, I guess I probably should have updated Anathema at some point after 2012. Also I would download your shameless plug if I had an android phone, a shame it's not a web-app (hint hint).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5618-quorumof4","name":"QuorumOf4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:16:53-07:00","id":476005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475666#post475666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Anathema is done, is there any talks about maybe doing a nWod/oWod system?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I, for one, wouldn't even know how to spell that. And in all honesty, &quot;done&quot;? It took us ten years to get to the current state of &quot;not done&quot;. :-/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:39:25-07:00","id":476027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475500#post475500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. This road has been open ever since we introduced the option to add custom Charm text.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool feature. It also makes me think about loading Anathema up with others' custom Charms. Would it be difficult for Anathema to help facilitate that? Something like... a homebrewer writes up a custom Charm in Anathema, hits a button to generate some bit of code to be pasted online, others can drop that code into a particular section of Anathema, and Anathema proceeds to populate a new custom Charm entry just as the original homebrewer had it.<br /> <br /> Dunno if there'd be a lot of call for it, but should the Wiki return, I could see some people appreciating a means to quickly harvest custom content like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:59:31-07:00","id":476093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475718#post475718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An essay separating model and view in PDFs</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds cool, color me interested. I'll PM you with further questions, lest this gets too detailed for a thread about EX3.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:12:27-07:00","id":476102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476027#post476027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be difficult for Anathema to help facilitate that? Something like... a homebrewer writes up a custom Charm in Anathema, hits a button to generate some bit of code to be pasted online, others can drop that code into a particular section of Anathema, and Anathema proceeds to populate a new custom Charm entry just as the original homebrewer had it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all difficult.<br /> Basic: As simple solution would just give you a text snippet to share for a single Charm and allow you to paste it somewhere next to that for processing.<br /> Add on: Checks whether the charm is valid and all prerequisites exist.<br /> Add on: Helps you to find charms for export.<br /> Add on: Allows to export a whole tree at once to make sure prerequisites exist.<br /> Luxury: A more comfortable solution also helps you with entering the Charm itself. (I tried building something like it once, but the result never satisfied me.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T14:05:25-07:00","id":476265,"title":"","content":"Will this version have the option for Personal Pictures and will there be a option for a full page picture or large option?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Like the Sun I am relentless even in death...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3293-rahod","name":"Rahod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T15:01:04-07:00","id":476328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475500#post475500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure what you mean by an &quot;UI&quot; - I thought it's a &quot;skin&quot; until I read the question below. Please clarify.</div> </div> </div> </div>User interface - which I've always took to mean the actual buttons, knobs and displays the user employed to interact with the device.<br /> <br /> I'm basically asking if all the buttons, graphs, drop-down menus and the like are going to be in different places than last time, and if you can customize where they all go.<br /> <br /> Thanks for answering our questions! Excelsior!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T15:22:36-07:00","id":476343,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the update! It's good to know what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T01:14:13-07:00","id":476759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>QuorumOf4</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=475979#post475979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I would download your shameless plug if I had an android phone, a shame it's not a web-app (hint hint).</div> </div> </div> </div>With Google's recent efforts to make android apps run in Chrome, this should only be a matter of weeks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rahod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476265#post476265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will this version have the option for Personal Pictures and will there be a option for a full page picture or large option?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Probably not at first, but we want to go there. We already have some frames and stuff in place, filled with placeholders!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476328#post476328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basically asking if all the buttons, graphs, drop-down menus and the like are going to be in different places than last time, and if you can customize where they all go.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we are actually thinking of the same thing, nice.<br /> Yes, we have changed much about the UI coming from Anathema 5. Things won't be customizable without deep knowledge of the system, though. If you see anything that should be different (or even customizable), we're eager for your feedback!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T01:41:05-07:00","id":476776,"title":"","content":"Don't suppose you've seen Empire: Legends, for use with Star-Wars Fantasy Flight Games? Is this new Anathema going to be something like that? I'm quite fond of it myself, even to the point I don't even use paper character sheets for our Edge of the Empire game anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T05:22:16-07:00","id":476843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476776#post476776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't suppose you've seen Empire: Legends, for use with Star-Wars Fantasy Flight Games? Is this new Anathema going to be something like that? I'm quite fond of it myself, even to the point I don't even use paper character sheets for our Edge of the Empire game anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just had a look at the Chrome App. It certainly is beautiful and evocative, until you get to editing data instead of just using it. Doesn't appear to be too helpful then, but I don't know the system and might be wrong on that count.<br /> So, Anathema will still be an editor first, not a stat's viewer, though we try to make getting to the data easier than before. Without an dedicated artist on the team, we won't get to their level, though. I know two or three people to talk to, but we can't actually work with anyone as long as the NDA is in place.<br /> Even though, I'd love to hear from people willing to help us with either the program or the website, which feels somewhat outdated as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T05:55:49-07:00","id":476846,"title":"","content":"Will Anathema continue to make your build choices optimal for you (e.g., when playing a Dawn with Integrity non-Favored, when you spend three of your 28 dots on War and then buy a dot in Integrity with bonus points, reroute the dot in Integrity to have been purchased with the initial 28 and buy the dot in War with a single bonus point, instead of the two it would've cost to get the dot in Integrity)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 04-11-2015, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T22:51:12-07:00","id":477555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476846#post476846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will Anathema continue to make your build choices optimal for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Was this ever up for debate?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T00:24:22-07:00","id":477627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=477555#post477555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Was this ever up for debate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe so, but the first time I used Anathema, it <i>did</i> kinda surprise me; I'd made a character on paper and made a mistake similar to my example, and hadn't noticed it until I'd plugged said character into Anathema.<br /> <br /> &quot;Where the hell is this extra bonus point coming from?&quot; I asked myself. &quot;Is it a bug?&quot; It took me a while to realize what had happened. &gt;.&gt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T18:04:27-07:00","id":478550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476843#post476843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just had a look at the Chrome App. It certainly is beautiful and evocative, until you get to editing data instead of just using it. Doesn't appear to be too helpful then, but I don't know the system and might be wrong on that count.<br /> So, Anathema will still be an editor first, not a stat's viewer, though we try to make getting to the data easier than before. Without an dedicated artist on the team, we won't get to their level, though. I know two or three people to talk to, but we can't actually work with anyone as long as the NDA is in place.<br /> Even though, I'd love to hear from people willing to help us with either the program or the website, which feels somewhat outdated as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well it is actually an editor that you can basically work with any time. And the simplification of certain things is dirt simple; in FFG Star Wars games you use a set of special dice to build up a pool, and when you're skilled in something you &quot;upgrade&quot; some dice to more beneficial ones. So in the app it represents this with little polygons the shape and color of the dice you use for a specific check. It's an odd duck system, but a good one, and very in the same kind of vein Exalted wants to be in.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T08:19:18-07:00","id":479061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=476759#post476759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Google's recent efforts to make android apps run in Chrome, this should only be a matter of weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dat google yo, dey so smert. <br /> <br /> That's cool, I was unaware of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5618-quorumof4","name":"QuorumOf4","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5618_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:26:44-07:00","id":479174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=478550#post478550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it is actually an editor that you can basically work with any time. And the simplification of certain things is dirt simple; in FFG Star Wars games you use a set of special dice to build up a pool, and when you're skilled in something you &quot;upgrade&quot; some dice to more beneficial ones. So in the app it represents this with little polygons the shape and color of the dice you use for a specific check. It's an odd duck system, but a good one, and very in the same kind of vein Exalted wants to be in.</div> </div> </div> </div>In that case, the Chrome app I looked at appears to be a bad representation of the experience on android. I'll have another look on my phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T18:56:56-07:00","id":479740,"title":"","content":"Look at Star Wars Legends, it's the best one I found, has cloud storage and saving, a transfer system, it won't auto upgrade characters for you and doesn't have the text built in, but you can write it down fine, read it any time, and it will keep track of your backstory for you too. It does basically everything a paper sheet will do for you, as well as a little more. Here's hoping Anathema's Android App will be much the same <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T22:07:18-07:00","id":483170,"title":"","content":"Would you be willing to seed or link to a legitimate torrent? My Internet connection is downright awful at the moment (12-15kb/s), so even the rather insubstantial download of 43.5MB is an hours-long trial that hopefully doesn't get interrupted (which necessitates a restart).<br /> <br /> Please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T23:42:42-07:00","id":483233,"title":"","content":"Sorry, Zeal, but whom are you talking to? What do you want to download? Anathema? Which version? Or Empire: Legend?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T01:50:30-07:00","id":483360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=483233#post483233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, Zeal, but whom are you talking to? What do you want to download? Anathema? Which version? Or Empire: Legend?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, Anathema, comrade; the most current version. I have a friend torrenting it to me now (at a breath-taking .2kb/sec <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), but she didn't post it publicly since it's your work. There's also the delicate point of it being an executable, so not having official sanction automatically makes it look suspect.<br /> <br /> If you had a torrent link or download from your site for the latest version of Anathema then it would be nice. I'm not sure if that would fit well for you, though, and I don't want to come across as demanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T13:24:57-07:00","id":483819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=479740#post479740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at Star Wars Legends, it's the best one I found, has cloud storage and saving, a transfer system, it won't auto upgrade characters for you and doesn't have the text built in, but you can write it down fine, read it any time, and it will keep track of your backstory for you too. It does basically everything a paper sheet will do for you, as well as a little more. Here's hoping Anathema's Android App will be much the same <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Had a look at it, I now understand somewhat better what you mean. As a replacement for paper sheets, it sure is marvellous!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T13:30:43-07:00","id":483822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=483360#post483360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, Anathema, comrade; the most current version. I have a friend torrenting it to me now (at a breath-taking .2kb/sec <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), but she didn't post it publicly since it's your work. There's also the delicate point of it being an executable, so not having official sanction automatically makes it look suspect. If you had a torrent link or download from your site for the latest version of Anathema then it would be nice. I'm not sure if that would fit well for you, though, and I don't want to come across as demanding.</div> </div> </div> </div>There always is the download on our site, but you sure know that and it doesn't quite help you due to your spurious connection. As for setting up a torrent, I wouldn't know anything about that. How do you go about it? And how do you make it look legit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T13:49:11-07:00","id":484842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=483822#post483822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There always is the download on our site, but you sure know that and it doesn't quite help you due to your spurious connection. As for setting up a torrent, I wouldn't know anything about that. How do you go about it? And how do you make it look legit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a bit new to it myself. It is helpful as a crowdsourcing tool, especially for freeware. What it does is create a much smaller file (such as 10kb) that has a hash (not sure if it's Md5 or what) of your file, along with some other metadata. People who download that torrent file can then use a Torrent client to seek out others who have the same file, and then basically download the bits in a peer-to-peer connection. It's secure because of the way the file is identified is through a unique hash; any alteration to a file will tell the others in the community that said file is not correct, and then it will be refused a download. Each client can check the hash of the file as it downloads... I think. There are helpfiles out there that are more eloquent and informative on the subject.<br /> <br /> I think uTorrent is the most reputable little client out there. It lets you create a Torrent file and then you &quot;seed&quot; the file; anyone else who downloads the Torrent file (a &quot;magnet&quot;) will look for others broadcasting the signal that they have the file in question, and then handshake and download. It would reduce the bandwidth load on your site if even 10 people hosted the file, and then it would only grow from there. That way the bandwidth load is spread out instead of focused on just your server.<br /> <br /> The way to make it legit would be to host the torrent seed (and maybe copy the hash output) to your website. That way people could just go to you for the legitimate &quot;seed&quot; file and then download from there.<br /> <br /> I don't know.. The more I think about it, the more I think I'm just in a rather unique, cruddy situation. It's taken about a week but I've almost downloaded it. The neat thing is that interruptions in the download don't corrupt the file, so that's nice. I think the bigger benefit is for very large files coming from someone with bandwidth concerns.<br /> <br /> I appreciate your attentiveness on the matter! It was nice being able to interact with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5706-zeal","name":"Zeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T00:20:55-07:00","id":485199,"title":"","content":"A while ago, I mentioned that you couldn't change Attributes freely in Anathema for Ex3.<br /> I looked, I thought, I typed, and presto: You can now define Attributes and Abilities freely. The system has some expectations, though, so if you choose to houserule Dodge away, your Dodge DV will plummet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T13:41:59-07:00","id":485671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=484842#post484842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think uTorrent is the most reputable little client out there. It lets you create a Torrent file and then you &quot;seed&quot; the file; anyone else who downloads the Torrent file (a &quot;magnet&quot;) will look for others broadcasting the signal that they have the file in question, and then handshake and download. It would reduce the bandwidth load on your site if even 10 people hosted the file, and then it would only grow from there. That way the bandwidth load is spread out instead of focused on just your server.</div> </div> </div> </div>uTorrent is most definitely not all that reputable at the moment, given the outrage surrounding the program's installation of a BitCoin miner on computers that had uTorrent installed. They've reportedly removed the miner from the latest version of uTorrent a few days ago, so you might want to check that you have said latest version. Personally, I've switched to <a href=\"http://dev.deluge-torrent.org/wiki/About\" target=\"_blank\">Deluge</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:42:46-07:00","id":486356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=485199#post485199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A while ago, I mentioned that you couldn't change Attributes freely in Anathema for Ex3.<br /> I looked, I thought, I typed, and presto: You can now define Attributes and Abilities freely. The system has some expectations, though, so if you choose to houserule Dodge away, your Dodge DV will plummet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hurray ! Related to that, since Abilities/Attributes are no longer hard coded, are static values ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T09:29:36-07:00","id":486468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=486356#post486356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since Abilities/Attributes are no longer hard coded, are static values ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the aforementioned Dodge DV? They still are, though I have already thought about making them freely defineable. We have half of the engine for that in place anyway, because we need to parse Essence pool formulas.<br /> Liberating Abilities and Attributes was a nice side effect on my way to another goal, and dealing with static values as well would not help me reach it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What would you do if they were? What would it help you with?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","user":"urskr","date":".  Typos 04-27-2015, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T06:53:14-07:00","id":488215,"title":"","content":"I think there's an Infernal Charm off of Mind Hand Manipulation that lets you parry with Manipulation+Essence or something. I could just be making that up, could be <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Charms:Force-Suppression_Barrier\" target=\"_blank\">Force Suppression Barrier</a> (I'm away from my library). However, there's always the homebrew case of Charms/Artifacts/Merits/ST rule 0's that have static values formula components subbed out for other things.<br /> <br /> Personally I would find that an optional upgrade, but it wouldn't be useless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T00:05:07-07:00","id":492382,"title":"","content":"Status update: One of the puzzles mentioned initially is solved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T17:04:06-07:00","id":493016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=492382#post492382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Status update: One of the puzzles mentioned initially is solved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yay!<br /> <br /> Can I say I'm very happy you're posting updates to the forum? It's really appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:30:38-07:00","id":493271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korhal_IV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=493016#post493016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I say I'm very happy you're posting updates to the forum? It's really appreciated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I found the update somewhat useless myself, since it doesn't say anything but &quot;we're working on it, trust us.&quot;<br /> But if it helps you, that's cool.<br /> <br /> Here's some more substance to go with yesterday's soup: 4. That is the number of currently known major puzzlers that we still have to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:34:54-07:00","id":493274,"title":"","content":"Well, you guys are basically volunteers working on an NDA. You're not obligated to post anything at all. So just letting us know that &quot;Hey, I think we might be X% closer to being done!&quot; is an effort on your part that you don't need to do, so a thanks is appropriate. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-26T22:42:44-07:00","id":493303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=493271#post493271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I found the update somewhat useless myself, since it doesn't say anything but &quot;we're working on it, trust us.&quot;<br /> But if it helps you, that's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think we make a thread for each Monday Meeting update? :P<br /> <br /> Just reading that progress on something is a good feeling. It's like watching the loading bar move when a computer is downloading or installing something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T09:37:41-07:00","id":493698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=486468#post486468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like the aforementioned Dodge DV? They still are, though I have already thought about making them freely defineable. We have halve of the engine for that in place anyway, because we need to parse Essence pool formulas.<br /> Liberating Abilities and Attributes was a nice side effect on my way to another goal, and dealing with static values as well would not help me reach it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: What would you do if they were? What would it help you with?</div> </div> </div> </div>Future proofing mostly ! We don't know how future splats and even the core rules are gonna change a few years down the line. The less that's hard coded the easier it is to adjust for future (and custom) supplements/systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=493271#post493271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I found the update somewhat useless myself, since it doesn't say anything but &quot;we're working on it, trust us.&quot;<br /> But if it helps you, that's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Open dialog (even if behind an NDA) is a good thing. Discussions that say &quot;We're working on it&quot; are better than the nebulous and aging announcements that say the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1759-kawaiiwolf","name":"kawaiiwolf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1759_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:56:23-07:00","id":493748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kawaiiwolf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=493698#post493698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Future proofing mostly ! We don't know how future splats and even the core rules are gonna change a few years down the line. The less that's hard coded the easier it is to adjust for future (and custom) supplements/systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are two risks involved here: One is not getting Anathema ready in time, one is not being able to support future changes to the system. Right now, as far as they are exclusive, we prefer to reduce the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Open dialog (even if behind an NDA) is a good thing. Discussions that say &quot;We're working on it&quot; are better than the nebulous and aging announcements that say the same. </div> </div> </div>Okay, got it. Will keep all of you posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:48:10-07:00","id":498334,"title":"","content":"Solved another puzzler, thank's to one of Vestrial's great ideas. Three puzzlers remain, but it gets harder from here on out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T22:55:16-07:00","id":498336,"title":"","content":"Would it be violating the NDA to tell us what these puzzles are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:07:25-07:00","id":498360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=498336#post498336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be violating the NDA to tell us what these puzzles are?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, since each of them revolves around introducing a 3E rule into the program.<br /> Please trust in that I am telling you all I am allowed to tell you.<br /> <br /> If the changes had been revealed elsewhere, I could speak openly, but I don't know if they are and the web is far too noisy to find information like that and ascertain that the revelation is legitimate. Probably applies to all kinds revelations in all kinds of situations, now that I think of it, but we can leave that for philosophy class.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:10:45-07:00","id":498362,"title":"","content":"Great to hear that stuff is going on though! Maybe we won't get anathema for launch but unless something terrible happens we'll probably get it within a few months of release right? Assuming the release is also within a few months of now anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:11:21-07:00","id":498364,"title":"","content":"No worries! I thought that it might be the case, but hadn't seen anything to confirm or deny it, so I was just curious. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:26:32-07:00","id":498396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=498362#post498362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great to hear that stuff is going on though! Maybe we won't get anathema for launch but unless something terrible happens we'll probably get it within a few months of release right? Assuming the release is also within a few months of now anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I strongly assume so.<br /> Currently, I tend to just putting out whatever we have shortly after the book comes out, tell all of you &quot;these three points don't work right yet&quot;, have all of you yell at us &quot;there are three points that don't work yet&quot;, and take it from there. :-D<br /> We've been releasing unfinished and broken software ever since 2004, and look where it got us!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:40:55-07:00","id":498411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=498396#post498396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, I strongly assume so.<br /> Currently, I tend to just putting out whatever we have shortly after the book comes out, tell all of you &quot;these three points don't work right yet&quot;, have all of you yell at us &quot;there are three points that don't work yet&quot;, and take it from there. :-D<br /> We've been releasing unfinished and broken software ever since 2004, and look where it got us!</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a great way to do it, even if it doesn't have the, I dunno whatever &quot;Maximum momentum&quot; stat or something, it's just more easy and reliable than paper. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-30T23:44:56-07:00","id":498413,"title":"","content":"Stuff like that. A Charm being available in the program before the rules would allow you to learn it; some free option not fully exploited, costing you more points than it should.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:04:17-07:00","id":498657,"title":"","content":"I've a question, and I haven't used Anathema hardly at all (sorry, didn't even realize it existed until the Kickstarter) so maybe this is already available, but...<br /> <br /> Let's say I'm running a game where the PC's circle are part of a traveling circus, so I give everyone 5 extra abiltiy points to spend on Athletics, Larceny, Presence, or Performance. Is there an easy way to note that somewhere? (If not flagging those five points as part of the starting ability pool, then at least a notes field were the player can jot down &quot;had starting +y xp due to Circus Bonus&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-01T05:25:55-07:00","id":498698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=498657#post498657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've a question, and I haven't used Anathema hardly at all (sorry, didn't even realize it existed until the Kickstarter) so maybe this is already available, but...<br /> <br /> Let's say I'm running a game where the PC's circle are part of a traveling circus, so I give everyone 5 extra abiltiy points to spend on Athletics, Larceny, Presence, or Performance. Is there an easy way to note that somewhere? (If not flagging those five points as part of the starting ability pool, then at least a notes field were the player can jot down &quot;had starting +y xp due to Circus Bonus&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just ignore the red flags on the screen and spend five extra points on abilities. You know what you are doing, after all.<br /> <br /> Anathema does not enforce limits as a computer game would, since there are too many groups changing the rules in small ways like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T13:41:56-07:00","id":619348,"title":"","content":"As the 3E backer copy is hopefully coming out soon, at least it feels that way. Is there any update as to when you think the character generator will be ready? BTW- I'm a huge fan of your existing character generator for 2E. Thank you so much for your work!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Magma Kraken EVERYTHING!!!&quot; - A response fitting for any situation","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/162-mr_bony_hands","name":"Mr_Bony_Hands","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T15:07:47-07:00","id":625971,"title":"","content":"Will it still be in Java? Oracle seems to be going after anyone using it these days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/694-firemage","name":"Firemage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar694_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T00:52:39-07:00","id":672980,"title":"","content":"First off, thanks for the updates and bountiful feedback to our many questions.<br /> <br /> Question: Out of curiosity, why aren't you and your team being paid for making this program? I was one of the people that pushed for this to happen as a Kickstarter backer. I pushed as I did mainly because I believe in your program, and for your team to paid for a product that has been well received and used, almost, religiously (and happily) by many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6171-coyotekin","name":"Coyotekin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6171_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T02:41:47-07:00","id":673030,"title":"","content":"My 2 cents as exalted user and working developer:<br /> <br /> - they starts Anathema v1 as a free project<br /> - they did for pleasure and the greater goods and for exalted users<br /> <br /> Best reason imho:<br /> OP can't pay their team for a project of this size.<br /> Individuals paiement will probably never be enough to pay for this amount of work.<br /> <br /> Maybe they could ask for donation ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8010-alanis","name":"Alanis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T08:05:12-07:00","id":673181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alanis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=673030#post673030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My 2 cents as exalted user and working developer:<br /> <br /> - they starts Anathema v1 as a free project<br /> - they did for pleasure and the greater goods and for exalted users<br /> <br /> Best reason imho:<br /> OP can't pay their team for a project of this size.<br /> Individuals paiement will probably never be enough to pay for this amount of work.<br /> <br /> Maybe they could ask for donation ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would totally donate toward the project! I love their 2.5ed creation tool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Magma Kraken EVERYTHING!!!&quot; - A response fitting for any situation","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/162-mr_bony_hands","name":"Mr_Bony_Hands","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T09:04:16-07:00","id":673236,"title":"","content":"Hey, everyone, thanks for the replies over these last few days.<br /> The latest news is the same as the news before, we didn't do much over the last month. I could list reasons now, but you will all know them.<br /> <br /> As for us being paid for the work, it is as Alanis said. Once money comes into play, I would start to wonder whether it is actually enough, and people would be entitled to all kinds of weird expectations, such as us actually delivering something by a predetermined point in time.<br /> Donations, now, that's something different. Despite my best promises to never pay for this project, I caved at some point and rented a server to host our builds and downloads. Sharing that cost would be very welcome. (Although it would probably keep me from changing to a more sensible infrastructure indefinitely.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:21:12-07:00","id":673310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=673236#post673236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, everyone, thanks for the replies over these last few days.<br /> The latest news is the same as the news before, we didn't do much over the last month. I could list reasons now, but you will all know them.<br /> <br /> As for us being paid for the work, it is as Alanis said. Once money comes into play, I would start to wonder whether it is actually enough, and people would be entitled to all kinds of weird expectations, such as us actually delivering something by a predetermined point in time.<br /> Donations, now, that's something different. Despite my best promises to never pay for this project, I caved at some point and rented a server to host our builds and downloads. Sharing that cost would be very welcome. (Although it would probably keep me from changing to a more sensible infrastructure indefinitely.)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you throw a Paypal button or something up on your site I'll see if I can scrape a donation together. It's the least I can do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T12:13:35-07:00","id":673341,"title":"","content":"How much does your server cost for a year? I'd probably be willing to pay a year or two simply to support this wonderful app which saved a gaming night more than once","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T13:54:01-07:00","id":673411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=673236#post673236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, everyone, thanks for the replies over these last few days.<br /> The latest news is the same as the news before, we didn't do much over the last month. I could list reasons now, but you will all know them.<br /> <br /> As for us being paid for the work, it is as Alanis said. Once money comes into play, I would start to wonder whether it is actually enough, and people would be entitled to all kinds of weird expectations, such as us actually delivering something by a predetermined point in time.<br /> Donations, now, that's something different. Despite my best promises to never pay for this project, I caved at some point and rented a server to host our builds and downloads. Sharing that cost would be very welcome. (Although it would probably keep me from changing to a more sensible infrastructure indefinitely.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What Kyman201 said - where can we donate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T15:25:22-07:00","id":676891,"title":"","content":"First, [not-poorly written thanks to everyone involved on the creation of Anathema]<br /> <br /> <s>Second, can I ask for help regarding an error message here?</s> Never mind, deleted characters and started working again<br /> <br /> Edit: Third, any chance for an option to break the limits? Like, when it's ticked/on/enabled any character can choose from any charms, or any backgrounds, or things like that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","user":"imadaman","date":". 09-26-2015, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8011-imadaman","name":"imadaman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8011_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:47:59-07:00","id":734438,"title":"","content":"Can we get another update now that 3rd edition is actually out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1521-jang","name":"Jang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1521_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-28T05:50:50-07:00","id":734446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=734438#post734438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get another update now that 3rd edition is actually out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it's not, it's only the backer preview","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T07:26:43-08:00","id":749122,"title":"","content":"is it possible to have a tentative eta for anathema? or can we get an update to know where its at? seeing as the backers copies have been released already itd be nice to know how far along you guys are =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1364-nemo_oceansoul","name":"Nemo_Oceansoul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T14:12:50-08:00","id":750084,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Paradox's acquisition of White Wolf might have an effect on Anathema. They are a software company, they might want to make supporting software for the tabletop games themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-02T15:11:20-08:00","id":750171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=750084#post750084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Paradox's acquisition of White Wolf might have an effect on Anathema. They are a software company, they might want to make supporting software for the tabletop games themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how Paradox handles things but most tabletop rpg companies have no problem with game aid and character creation/managing software as long as it free and no money is made from it. In fact the only tabletop company that I know that doesn't allow such things is WotC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/23580224/t4q8xrt1.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/816-leo1925","name":"leo1925","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar816_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T14:15:04-08:00","id":760205,"title":"","content":"they [WotC] are also famous for suing fan artists for making fan art of their characters. so yah x)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1364-nemo_oceansoul","name":"Nemo_Oceansoul","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T18:16:18-08:00","id":761092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jorlem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=750084#post750084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if Paradox's acquisition of White Wolf might have an effect on Anathema. They are a software company, they might want to make supporting software for the tabletop games themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever met the modding community of The Paradox Games? I wouldn't worry.<br /> The designers are encouraged by the bosses to help modders make third party content for their games. They consider it good business","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T21:33:32-08:00","id":761226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=761092#post761092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever met the modding community of The Paradox Games? I wouldn't worry.<br /> The designers are encouraged by the bosses to help modders make third party content for their games. They consider it good business</div> </div> </div> </div>I've <i>made</i> mods for CK2, I know how amazingly supportive they are of modders. I'm also aware that, by their own rules, mods for their games are only allowed to be available for download via their forum, or Steam, that enabling or duplicating DLC content for those that do not own the DLC is forbidden, and that things posted to their forum are legally theirs (This is the same as the state of homebrew was on the old WW forum, by the way. Not sure if that is the case here. It is mainly to avoid IP arguments if a DLC does something that was done in an existing mod. Again, this is the same reason the old WW forum had nigh-identical boilerplate.)<br /> <br /> I was more thinking of the possibility that they might want to create a program that does the same things that does what Anathema is intended to do, and that unlike mods to their games, Anathema is not under PI's umbrella. (That Anathema was promised by the Kickstarter likely goes a very long way, though. I'd be willing to bet that existing &quot;contracted out&quot; stuff like this will be one of the things talked about in whatever negotiations happen between PI/WW and Onyx Path.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />If you want to play Thomas Edison, you'd better be up to the task of carrying all of civilization through the Renaissance and Industrial Revolution, <i>while the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded are shooting at you</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/591-jorlem","name":"Jorlem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar591_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:51:22-08:00","id":773290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=734438#post734438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we get another update now that 3rd edition is actually out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I have just published our work-in-progress code at <a href=\"https://github.com/anathema/anathema_3e\" target=\"_blank\">https://github.com/anathema/anathema_3e</a>.<br /> <br /> (Two lines of tech talk ahead:<br /> Everyone who is interested in contributing is welcome to send pull requests.<br /> Please note: This is a new repository with a rewritten history, so old forks will not be compatible.)<br /> <br /> The main puzzlers are still unresolved, so the release is still some time off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T11:53:44-08:00","id":773292,"title":"","content":"Regarding Paradox, I have not spoken to Rich whether this changes anything. Last thing I now are some limitations put down by CCP the very day before the Paradox deal went public, and I will abide by these until Anathema for 3e has matured to a state where they actually matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T17:15:32-08:00","id":773523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=773290#post773290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main puzzlers are still unresolved, so the release is still some time off.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are those? I looked at the repository and there was no obvious list of issues or unsupported features.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T10:52:01-08:00","id":774121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=773523#post773523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are those? I looked at the repository and there was no obvious list of issues or unsupported features.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, sorry. Since we had to keep things under wraps until very recently, they are stored on a private Trello board.<br /> The main things are:<br /> * To learn the Martial Arts excellency when you favor Martial Arts and put a dot in it<br /> * To allow for Martial Arts to be selected as the Supernal Ability<br /> * Solar XP<br /> * Control spells for sorcery<br /> * Not counting direct prerequisites for prereqs \u00e0 la &quot;Charm X and any 3 other Archery Charms&quot;<br /> <br /> There are some more, but I consider them less relevant:<br /> * Shaping rituals in general<br /> * Craft in general<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:12:51-08:00","id":774140,"title":"","content":"Thanks. When I get the chance, I'll take a look through the codebase and take a crack at some of those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T11:44:14-08:00","id":774163,"title":"","content":"Cool. I am looking forward to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-27T20:09:10-08:00","id":775757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=774121#post774121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* To allow for Martial Arts to be selected as the Supernal Ability</div> </div> </div> </div>Before: how complicated could this be?<br /> After: ahhh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T01:14:17-08:00","id":775858,"title":"","content":"I wish I coul