ituals in general<br /> * Craft in general</div> </div> </div> </div>Sudden thought: Another problem you might want to consider: there is the charm Exegesis of the Distilled Form, which provides regular XP that doesn't count towards Essence growth; that'll be something to consider. I'll spend today digging around the code and learning it's intricaticies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/650-dtemplar5","name":"DTemplar5","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar650_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T09:21:37-08:00","id":776061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DTemplar5</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=776008#post776008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sudden thought: Another problem you might want to consider: there is the charm Exegesis of the Distilled Form, which provides regular XP that doesn't count towards Essence growth; that'll be something to consider. I'll spend today digging around the code and learning it's intricaticies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I've made a note of it. I consider rules for specific Charms of secondary importance compared to general rules, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Before: how complicated could this be?<br /> After: ahhh. </div> </div> </div>What specifically did you encounter? Maybe we can resolve things by looking at them jointly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T11:05:35-08:00","id":776102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nemo_Oceansoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=760205#post760205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they [WotC] are also famous for suing fan artists for making fan art of their characters. so yah x)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there are <i>so many</i> DeviantArt accounts filled with fanart of Urza, Elminster and the Great Dalmuti. <br /> Fandom is the bloodflow of entertainment properties. Crush its expression, and the only things keeping your game world/TV series/movie franchise/fantasy or SF setting/comic book title, etc. from ossifying completely are new releases. And even with a steady flow of well-received new content, stomping things like fanart, fanmods, or fan-accessories (think Wookiepedia or Ed'sExalted) serves only to blunt enthusiasm and diminish engagement in return for the illusion of control gained by &quot;safeguarding the property&quot; from those who care most about it.<br /> <br /> Sorry, personal ragepoint of mine. Back to Anathema 3E updates and comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:04:45-08:00","id":776616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=776061#post776061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What specifically did you encounter? Maybe we can resolve things by looking at them jointly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that wasn't supposed to be a criticism! Not at all. Just that this looks like a very orthodox Java-y MVP setup and it can be difficult to encode a seemingly cross-cutting concern like the Brawl/MA dependence in a system like that once it's already been set up.<br /> <br /> And I think I know how to do it via hacking up the presenter? (And also the MA trait holder widget needs to subscribe to Brawl rather than simply return Brawl's state directly.) But haven't had a chance because I caught the flu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","user":"AtG","date":". 11-29-2015, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T10:35:47-08:00","id":776674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>39Steps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=776102#post776102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stomping things like Ed'sExalted</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything apart from WW not being interested in making a deal with Ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T12:32:59-08:00","id":776742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=776616#post776616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh that wasn't supposed to be a criticism! Not at all. Just that this looks like a very orthodox Java-y MVP setup and it can be difficult to encode a seemingly cross-cutting concern like the Brawl/MA dependence in a system like that once it's already been set up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't take it as such. Instead, I assumed that Anathema's structure is not self-explanatory if you have not spent the last 11 years with the code, since there are many experimental peculiarities and roads not (quite) traveled in there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/136-urskr","name":"urskr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T15:57:56-08:00","id":776854,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the updates, Urskr! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/K9a6Pmp.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/998-korhal_iv","name":"Korhal_IV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"592"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T11:30:46-08:00","id":777836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>urskr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/474023-state-of-anathema-for-third-edition?p=776674#post776674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything apart from WW not being interested in making a deal with Ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies. In my frothing irk-frenzy, I failed to make myself clear. I wasn't sniping at WW/Onyx Path for any sort of negativity towards Ed'sExalted--I was just using EE as an examle of an excellent and useful adjunct that's a fan-made labor of love, requiring countless hours of effort to create, and which only boosts the property it concerns-- I'd have put Anathema on that list, too, if it hadn't transitioned from fan-work to official WW/OP adjunct. AFAIK, WW has never had a problem with Ed's.<br /> <br /> It's when the property owners stomp things <i>like</i> Ed's Exalted, Wookiepedia, Bulbapedia, etc. that their short-sightedness punishes the fan-creator, deprives other fans of the work's utility, and ultimately diminishes their brand. WW was smart, and extended its offer to Anathema, without trying to take down Ed's. They recognized that there was room for multiple chargen programs, and for that I applaud them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1536-39steps","name":"39Steps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-03T21:31:30-08:00","id":779530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-i